From: Voice (claude/r7-audit-voice, whole-project audit 2026-11-09)
Subject: [PATCH 019] voice audit V-21 and V-40: the voicesig comment in turn.js; the child-text emit after the turn is authorised

Two findings from docs/design/round7/audit/voice.md that land in Brain's files.

V-21 (server/brain/turn.js): the comment above voicesigSeam.turn says a voice-signal state is shadow until the precision
gate passes. Since the owner's 2026-10-27 decision the default mode is `internal` (server/voicesig/lesson.js seamMode): a
computed state picks the plan's tie-breakers (followUpProbe, gentlerHint, slowerPace) in every lesson, on a placeholder
prior. Comment only; no behaviour change. The voice files' own comments were corrected on the voice branch.

V-40 (server/routes/lesson.js): POST /api/lesson/turn emitted the child's words to in-process child-text listeners
(server/duplex/childText.js) BEFORE lessonTurn ran, i.e. before the request was authorised for that lesson. The emit now
runs after lessonTurn returns. The voice branch made the same change in /api/lesson/turn-audio (server/routes/voice.js).
No listener is registered in the app today (Studio's M4 consumer is not wired), so nothing a child sees changes.
Pinned: tests/r7-audit-voice-server.test.mjs ("V-40") covers the voice route; for this route, a test that posts a turn
for a lesson the caller does not own and asserts no onChildText event fires.

